file","symbol":null,"symbol_cardinality":0},"role":"subject"}],"assurance":"inferred","author":{"authority":"agent","model":"unidentified","session":"unrecorded"},"body":{"claim":"A per-declaration rebuild here does not read as slow, it reads as a corpus this project cannot measure.","detail":"Anchor::capture fingerprints the whole tree and FileIndex::build indexes the whole file, so calling either inside the declaration loop costs a file with D declarations D full passes. On a 25,000-line C++ header that was twenty commits failing to finish in a hundred and ten seconds. The damage was not the runtime: replay is what substantiates G2, so the cost silently restricted the measured corpora to repositories small enough to tolerate it, and the shape it excluded is the single-header library that stresses the resolver hardest. The fingerprint table, the symbol table and the index are computed once per file pair. Anything added to this loop that takes a tree rather than a node belongs outside it."},"chain":"c5142c9b981c1e145e0dd64d34de88f17a58e792edffa360a17c2e89b49a451f","created":1790250213,"kind":"known_failure_mode","lifecycle":"active","schema":1}
